  "id": "COMPOUND:31474 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (+)-Dihydrocarvone may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular pathways. The compound is identified as a target for CD70 antigen, which in turn is a target of lidocaine and Gibberellin A19. These targets are all linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential downstream effect of (+)-Dihydrocarvone on this epigenetic regulator. The scores from the three paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with the highest score (0.6263) pointing to a direct interaction through CD70 antigen. The evidence highlights a possible mechanism where (+)-Dihydrocarvone influences the expression or activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex via the CD70 antigen pathway, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway underscores the complexity of the relationship and the need for further investigation to determine the precise molecular mechanisms involved.",
